      <title>Stylebase for Eclipse: sharing software architectural models</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Lightning Talks</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First, a very quick look at background information&#xA;(software architecture design,  modeling and patterns) would be taken, explaining the&#xA;benefits of maintaining an architectural knowledge base. Then the vision and current status of our project will be described. We would tell&#xA;about what the software can do at the moment and how we plan to improve&#xA;it in the future. If desired, a nice looking recorded demo can be shown.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Stylebase for Eclipse is tool for sharing and reusing software&#xA;architectural knowledge. Stylebase for Eclipse helps to maintain a&#xA;knowledge base of software architectural  models. The knowledge base can&#xA;store architectural patterns,  design patterns, reference architectures,&#xA;macro and micro architectures et cetera. Each model is associated with&#xA;HTML-formatted textual documentation and a number of searchable&#xA;properties. Users can maintain both local and shared repository and&#xA;download/upload models between the two.  Please visit &#xA;http:&lt;i&gt;stylebase.tigris.org &amp;lt;http:&lt;/i&gt;stylebase.tigris.org/&amp;gt;  for source&#xA;code and more information.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
